<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
	Count badge shown on the HUD diplomacy button.
	Copied from vanilla hud_campaign.twui.xml > label_missions_count (same image, font and
	docking) without its context callbacks. It is interactive: it shows its own tooltip
	(the deal list) and forwards clicks to the diplomacy button. Text, tooltip and
	visibility are set from script.
	States use the vanilla button names and the badge has the vanilla "Button" callback,
	so the engine itself switches them on mouse over and click (no script involved; the
	game doesn't send ComponentMouseOn/Off for it): active, down_off and inactive = normal,
	hover and down = brighter badge_hover.png, white text. Without the "Button" callback
	the badge only followed the diplomacy button's state (its StatePropagatorCallback).
	A build whose normal state was named "NewState" got stuck in "hover" after a click:
	the engine returns to "active", which didn't exist then.
-->
